  "cross_cloud_origin": null,
  "description": "This is a technique for isolating phage from agar plates.  When working with lytic phage, well-isolated, cleared areas in a lawn of bacteria (called plaques) are removed from the agar (by coring with a sterile pipette) and used to infect fresh bacteria in liquid medium.  The lysed culture can be used for a new plaque assay after 0.2 um filtering to remove residual bacteria.  New phage are &#34;plaque-purified&#34; a minimum of three times before they are considered to be free of other phage.",
